NOT RUN (the person who wrote the sheet)
  - THE EMAs: the Template's own, on 15-minute closes since 00:00 ET, seeded with the day's first close (an EMA(50) at 10:00 rests on about 40 bars); the slope is the EMA(50) now vs one bar before.
  - THE STOP is fixed in points (the family's structure stop, the pullback bar's extreme, is not used).
  - CAPPED PER SESSION PASS, NOT PER DAY: nyam, mid and pm are three passes, so a day can hold up to 3 trades and a trade of one pass may still be open when another pass enters; 'first tag' means the first of each pass.
  - COSTS AND FILLS: the engine's own (1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, $4 a round turn, tick replay).
  - FLAT: every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on half days); no entry in the last 5 minutes of a pass.
  - THE TEST DAYS (2025-07-01 on) ARE NOT READ by this sheet: build days only; the 3:1 block walk-forward comes later under PREREG.

ALSO TRUE OF THE RUN (the lane)
  - CAPPED PER SESSION PASS, NOT PER DAY: max_trades 1 counts inside each pass (3 passes: nyam, mid, pm), so a day can hold up to 3 trades; a family's own loss or trade count (none) counts inside one pass too.
  - The passes are independent: a trade of one pass may still be open when another pass enters (one position at a time holds inside a pass only).
  - Every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on an equity half day); no entry in the last 5 minutes of a pass.
  - Costs: $4.00 a round turn and 1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, 1 contract (the engine's own).

HONEST LIMITS
  - One video's rule, read on the build days (2021-09-22 .. 2025-06-30): in-sample.
  - The family's settings and the exits are the video's own: nothing was tuned, searched or picked.
  - The neighbours are shown to see how fragile the rule is; they are not alternatives to choose from.
  - The unseen days (2025-07-01 on) were not read: a person has to ask for that, and it is read once.
  - The random entries are the pipeline's own (any bar of the session pass, matched by day and pass): they do not wait for the family's entry window.
